{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792336985,"nonce":"rZfc/6Ob6k/+pI7xgmfA8v2vlu8=","title":"Host-made fibers: one i64 in and out, and no stack size","message":"zyntax_embed fiber.rs:52 creates the fiber with krio_fiber_new(entry, 0), the default stack (64 KiB in krio-fiber), with no way to ask for more; an overflow is a guard-page SIGSEGV (zylua reserves 64 MiB through new_with_env). Yields are 62-bit ints (fiber_backend.rs:207), resume_with takes one i64, and the tiered API decodes only Int or Bool (tiered.rs:441). Typed values in and out of a host-driven fiber are not possible.\n\nReported from RayDE's RayScript planning (RayDE git-bug 971d58e, latest comment); claims marked verified were checked in the code at 5c58f753, the rest come from a read-only review and their line numbers may drift.","files":null}]}